ns  really welcomed the court censure very  strong  censure of the government they said that  suspending the laws isn't enough because  they don't trust that the laws will go  away if they're just halted if their  implementation is halted  and they're reiterating their demand  that these laws  be repealed they're also reluctant to  take part in any committees because  they've been negotiating with the  government for weeks now and there's  been  no breakthrough so far the government  meanwhile has said has told the court  that these laws were passed after two  decades of deliberations that they  weren't rushed through  it says farmers are happy with them  because it gives them more options  that they have been engaging with  farmers the court listened to all of  this  and also to the uh reluctance by farmers  to take part in any committee and it  said that it didn't want to hear that  that it's trying to solve the situation  and the alternative for farmers  is to protest indefinitely  all right elizabeth i'm there thank you  so much for that update
 

